Significance: minor
Type: deprecated

Hooks keep v1's linked_orders_for_woocommerce/ root. Six keep their v1 names and fire once: post_type/supported_order_types, post_type/valid_statuses_for_new_child, node/status_name, node/can_create_child, autocompletion/should_autocomplete and autocompletion/completed_status. Each other v1 name still fires first, deprecated: create_linked_order_args (now linked_order/creation_args), created_linked_order (now linked_order/created), node/get_formatted_name (now node/formatted_name), metabox_output/after_add_new_child_button (now meta_box/after_add_new_child_button), list_table_output/column/insert_after (now list_table/preceding_column), list_table_output/column/content (now list_table/column_content), the general and plugin groups' get_group_fields (use woocommerce_get_settings_advanced), whose fields stay keyed by their v1 ids and keep an id they set, and the get_validated_option_value filters (now settings/validated_value).
